.TH PYCOMPILE 1 "October 2026" "pycompile 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pycompile \- compile Python source into a standalone native binary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pycompile
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIINPUT\fR [\-\- \fIPROGRAM_ARGS\fR...]
.br
.B pycompile
.B man
[\fB\-\-install\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pycompile
is an ahead-of-time compiler that translates a supported subset of Python directly into C,
invokes the platform C compiler, and emits a single standalone native executable. There is no
interpreter and no runtime dependency: the resulting binary runs on its own.
.PP
It is designed for small command-line programs and scripts where you want Python's syntax and
speed of iteration but a portable native binary as the deliverable.
.SH QUICK START
.PP
Compile a single file to a native binary named after the source:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile hello.py
.fi
.RE
.PP
Choose an output path explicitly:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile hello.py \-o build/hello
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile and immediately run the program:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile \-r hello.py
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile and also keep the generated C for inspection:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile hello.py \-\-emit\-c hello.c \-\-keep\-temps
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile a whole project directory that contains
.BR main.py :
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile ./myproject \-o myproject
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pass arguments to the compiled program after
.BR \-\- :
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile cli.py \-o cli \-\- \-\-verbose file.txt
.fi
.RE
.SH INPUT
.TP
.I INPUT
A
.B .py
file, or a directory containing
.B main.py
or
.BR __main__.py .
.PP
When
.I INPUT
is a directory,
.B pycompile
looks for
.B main.py
first, then
.BR __main__.py ,
and compiles that file as the program entry point.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Output binary path (default: input name without extension).
.TP
.B \-\-emit\-c " " \fIPATH\fR
Also write the generated C source to
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-temps
Keep the temporary C build directory.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-run
Compile and immediately run the program.
.TP
.B \-\-man
Print this manual to the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B man
Print this manual to the terminal.
.TP
.B man \-\-install
Install the man page. May require root privileges.
.TP
.B man \-\-prefix " " \fIDIR\fR
Install into
.IR DIR /share/man/man1
instead of
.IR /usr/local/share/man/man1 .
.SH LANGUAGE SUPPORT
The following Python features compile to native code:
.IP \(bu 2
Integer, float, string and boolean literals, and
.BR None .
.IP \(bu 2
f-strings with format specs and the
.B !r
conversion.
.IP \(bu 2
Lists, tuples, sets and dicts, including literal and comprehension forms.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR if ", " elif ", " else ", " while ", " for -in ", " break ", " continue ", " pass .
.IP \(bu 2
.B def
with default parameters, recursion, and
.B *args
and
.B **kwargs
parameters.
.IP \(bu 2
Calls with positional, keyword, 
.B *
and
.B **
arguments.
.IP \(bu 2
Chained comparisons,
.BR in ", " not in ", " is ", " is not ", " and ", " or ", " not .
.IP \(bu 2
Slicing and item assignment, augmented assignment.
.IP \(bu 2
.B %
string formatting (positional and mapping forms, flags, width, precision).
.IP \(bu 2
.BR lambda
expressions, nested functions and closures (including late binding).
.IP \(bu 2
.BR try ", " except ", " except " ... " as ", " else ", " finally ", " raise ", " assert ,
and catchable built-in exception types.
.IP \(bu 2
Stable
.B sort
and
.B sorted
with
.B reverse=True
and
.BR key= .
.IP \(bu 2
.B class
definitions with methods,
.BR __init__ ,
class and instance attributes, single inheritance,
.BR isinstance ,
and the
.BR __str__ , " " __repr__ , " " __eq__ , " " __len__ , " " __getitem__ , " " __setitem__
and
.B __contains__
protocols.
.IP \(bu 2
The
.B math
and
.B sys
modules.
.PP
The following are not yet supported and produce a clear compile error:
.IP \(bu 2
.BR super() ,
multiple inheritance and decorators.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR with ,
generators,
.B async
and
.BR await .
.IP \(bu 2
.BR return ", " break " or " continue
inside a
.B try
that has a
.B finally
clause.
.IP \(bu 2
Modules other than
.B math
and
.BR sys .
.SH RUNTIME MODEL
The generated C links against a small runtime library that is embedded by the compiler.
Values are heap-allocated tagged objects. A conservative mark-and-sweep garbage collector
reclaims unreachable objects by scanning the C stack, the program's globals and a few
runtime roots; unreachable reference cycles are collected too. Because the scan is
conservative, an object can occasionally be kept alive a little longer than strictly
necessary. Runtime errors print a Python-style traceback to stderr and exit with status 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Compile a hello-world script:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile hello.py
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile a project entry point to an explicit name:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile \-o demo app/main.py
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compile and run with arguments:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile \-r script.py \-\- 1 2 3
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep the generated C source:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pycompile script.py \-\-emit\-c script.c
.fi
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CC
Preferred C compiler to invoke. Falls back to
.BR cc ", " gcc ", " clang ", " tcc ,
then
.BR cl .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to any value to disable ANSI color in the terminal manual.
.TP
.B TERM=dumb
Disables color in the terminal manual.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success: the binary was produced, or the compiled program exited 0.
.TP
.B 1
Compile error, or the compiled program exited non-zero.
.TP
.B 2
Command line usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/pycompile.1
Installed manual page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR cc (1),
.BR gcc (1),
.BR clang (1),
.BR python3 (1)
.SH BUGS AND LIMITATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
The garbage collector is conservative: it may keep an unreachable object alive a little
longer than necessary, and it scans the whole C stack on each collection.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR super() ,
multiple inheritance and decorators are not supported.
.IP \(bu 2
A return, break or continue inside a try that has a finally clause is rejected at
compile time.
.IP \(bu 2
An uncaught exception prints a single-line traceback without file and line frames.
